      - armament: air_strike
        source: air strike LeO H-470
        aircraft_param: PFAD903_ASW_T10
        rate:
          stat: air strike LeO H-470 fire starts per minute
          unit: fires/min
          builds:
            base:
              fires_per_minute: 6.72
              fire_chance_pct: 28
              projectiles_per_minute: 24
            best:
              value:
                fires_per_minute: 6.72
                fire_chance_pct: 28
                projectiles_per_minute: 24
              assumed: []
    note: "Fire starts are theoretical: fires_per_minute = projectiles_per_minute x fire_chance, every projectile hitting a target that can burn. The headline is against one distant target at the bearing (degrees off the bow, clockwise) where the most fires start: the server gives each secondary mount its own target, and a gun fires at a target only when its mount turns to it outside its dead zones, so one target draws the mounts whose firing sectors cover its bearing, usually one side and the centerline. all_mounts_ceiling is every gun mount firing at once, which no single target sees. by_bearing gives the figure at standard bearings, starboard and its port mirror, on the base and best builds. salvo_fire_chance_pct = 1 - (1 - p)^n over the n bearing shells of one salvo. Not applied: the target's fire resistance and hull fire-node probability, the limit of fires burning at once, fire duration, dispersion and signal flags. Guns fire at their reload. A carrier squadron, which makes several attacks per sortie, attacks with attackerSize planes every attackCooldown, the shortest time between two of its attacks, while it has attacks left; flight to the target, returns and lost planes are left out, so this is its rate over the target. A squadron that attacks once per sortie, as hybrid ships launch them, attacks again when the hangar has restored its planes. An air strike releases every plane's ordnance once per consumable reload; its charges are not counted. Ordnance per attack is attackerSize x attackCount x projectilesPerAttack, the client's bombs per plane (PreprocessedPlanes). total adds the main battery's best ammo type, every secondary group, the best squadron of the stock plane modules (a carrier flies one at a time) and the best air strike aircraft (one air strike's aircraft share its charges)."
